I am beautiful what does it mean to you  when you hear these words do you truly  believe that you are beautiful without  trying to want to be someone else ladies  it is International Women's Day today  and I want each and every one of you to  know that you are beautiful and that you  are enough so being in the health and  fitness industry where unfortunately the  outer appearance seem to be the  number-one obsession with most people I  find that it is very important for us to  know that beauty is beyond skin deep so  I just want to take the time to share my  experiences and tips on how to build a  better body image especially with the  heavy influence of social media nowadays  the first tip is to be aware of your  influences so how many of you are on  Instagram Facebook or snapchat how often  do you check your social updates every  day or every hour well guys I just want  to start by saying that I don't think  social media is negative it is just a  medium for people you and me to convey  our message we the users have the  ultimate control on what we choose to  put out and also the messages or images  that we choose to take in so the people  whom you choose to follow have a huge  impact on your body image and also  self-esteem whether you're aware of it  or not every images and every messages  that you read everyday will either add  value to your life and make you feel  inspired and positive or let's face it  sometimes it will make you feel less  about yourself and [ __ ] about your life  so personally I am very selective over  whom I choose to follow on social media  I tend to follow friends or family  members and only people whom I know will  add value to my life and people whom I'm  always inspired by so I don't follow a  lot of people because I don't really  want to skirt through my Instagram or  Facebook every day just looking at  images of people who are just for  instance obsessed with how they look and  to be honest because social media is a  big part of my work and my life  as much as I can I only want to attract  things that will add value and will  continue to motivate me and inspire me  so just take the time to scroll through  your Instagram or Facebook page and ask  yourself why do you choose to follow him  or her is it because he has a very good  photography skill and I'm constantly  learning something new or is it because  she is motivating me and inspiring me if  so then by all means continue to be  inspired and influenced by them but if  however you feel that this person is not  adding any value to my life then  sometimes having the courage to remove  the negative vibes will actually help  you to build a better body image of  yourself the second tip is no more  comparisons be honest when your friends  or celebrities post pictures of their  perfect life dip down you might feel  envious and wish that your life were as  perfect as they are here's a fact what  you know about a person is only through  the lens most of the time it is never  100% true  they would portray their lives as how  they would want you to perceive it or  are you hooked over the number of likes  you get or are you envious of someone  you know who might have more followers  than you have based on my personal  experience I used to pay a lot of  attention to the number of likes I get  when I post up an image and if the  picture doesn't get as many likes as I  hope I would feel that you know what it  might be a bad post and sometimes you  can get so hooked and influenced by what  you think your followers would like to  see you ended up creating a fake reality  or an edited reality just to get the  number of likes up of course having  engagement from you guys is great I love  reading all your comments and all your  feedbacks but I have to remind myself  not to get hooked on the lights so  nowadays whenever I share a picture I  would always ask myself what is it that  I'm just trying to convey to my  followers will it add value to their  lives  it influenced them and motivate them in  a positive manner does it reflect the  real me and my world so I believe that  social media can be a very powerful and  positive platform for you and me to  share our messages and share our life  stories but it shouldn't be used as a  platform for you to compare yourself  with others and for you to feel less  about yourself we all came from  different backgrounds and we all have  different life stories and that is what  makes us unique and beautiful the third  tip is know your values in order to  build a more positive by the image  you've got to know your values know  yourself and embrace that so for  instance when it comes to exercising ask  yourself why is staying fit so important  to you is it because you're overweight  and you know that you need to lose  weight for your health is it because it  makes you feel good gives you more  energy and gives you more  self-confidence or is it just purely a  vanity thing if it's just pure vanity no  matter how fit and how good you look  from the outside I can assure you you  will never feel good by yourself and you  will never be happy so being in the  health and fitness industry I can tell  you that there are a lot of good-looking  people who look really fit on the  outside and you know what a lot of  people wish that they have their bodies  but these people are just constantly  self-sabotaging  and you always hear the negative  self-talk so oh my god you know I feel  so fat oh my God my thighs are so big oh  my god I've eaten so much today it is  just constant self-sabotaging because  they're basing their values on what they  look on the outside not what's on the  inside so when I first got into this  industry I would say that subconsciously  I was drawn into this car as well I saw  food as something negative something  that would cause me to gain weight  rather than something that would nourish  my body and no matter how much I've  progressed in my workout it is always  never good enough or I would still look  into the mirror and feel fat okay it's  it wasn't a good time and when I started  to look deep within and started to  embrace my values and when I started to  surround myself with people who aspired  to live a healthier and happier life  from within not just on the outside I  find that I became more at peace with  myself and that I became happier and in  fact I became more in love with fitness  this leads on to my next point which is  to love yourself  what does loving yourself means it  doesn't mean that you know this is who I  am and you can't change that I'm going  to look after myself too bad if you  don't like it or I'm going to do  whatever that makes me feel happy  and I don't really care how you feel  loving yourself  doesn't mean any of that in fact it  means that you know you're responsible  for your self-worth emotionally  physically and mentally you look after  yourself a new workout because you know  that you're responsible for your  well-being you don't find a need to  compare yourself with others or sick of  validation from others you know that  you're not your height your body weight  or how flat your tummy is and most  importantly you're able to forgive  yourself and be kind to yourself once  you start to embrace your values and  love yourself you will find more balance  in your life attract more happiness and  more positive people into your life  so no more self sabotaging or negative  self-talk and the final tip is to create  a positive space as much as we can blame  the media and it's negative influences I  feel that we have a responsibility and  role to play as well if you're on social  media you too have the responsibility to  either spread positive messages or vice  versa so what I want to do for the next  four weeks is for us to create a  positive online space by sharing your  pictures your worlds inspirational  quotes and any uplifting messages okay  so this may not only empower you but it  can also inspire your friends and also  follow us so I've listed 28 different  it's for each day remember there is no  right or wrong to this this is your  creative space so express yourself and  share with us what the word means to you  remember to hashtag I am beautiful and  Jaso inspiration make a profile public  so that we can all view your pictures  and stay inspired okay I will also be  selecting five winners who post Twitter  pictures continuously for the next 28  days to win my favorite tank top be  confident be happy beautiful okay take  this time and make this next four weeks  of the time for you to discover yourself  your values and to build a more positive  body image so get your family and  friends on board and inspire each other  remember to stay true to yourself  because I want to get to know the real  you okay and if you want to be part of a  more inspiring and more positive fitness  industry and if you want to become a  personal trainer then do check out the  National Academy of Sports Medicine  online personal training cause they are  currently offering a 14-day free trial  so take this opportunity to learn more  about fitness nutrition understanding  your clients and waist on becoming a  successful personal trainer and if you  find that you know what this is the  career path that I really want to go  down because I'm passionate to help  others in regards to health and  well-being then by all means sign up to  the full chorus okay click on the link  in my description box for more  information and I'm really excited to  see oil pictures for the next 28 days  let's create a more positive online  space so start posting and start  inspiring those around you all the best  you
 

